module main

# spec/todo.md item 19: a deferred-leaf result (an explicit-generic call with
# an omitted return type) used directly inside a `"{...}"` interpolation
# segment used to fail at lowering with "this interpolated expression was
# never resolved by the capability check" instead of printing a value,
# because `check_interpolated_string` demanded the segment's type before
# `finish_open_results` had pinned the call's still-open result leaf.

def identity[T](x: T):
    x

# The implicit-generic half of item 19: `add_one` has no `[T]` brackets at
# all, so whether it is generic is only known once its own body has been
# probed. `check_interpolated_string`'s `demand()` used to flush the leaf
# queue before that probe's verdict (`classify_param_decls`) was recorded,
# which permanently defaulted `x`'s still-open type while resolving
# `add_one`'s own deferred `+` obligation — turning `add_one` into an
# ordinary `int32` function instead of the implicit generic its body makes
# it, so lowering rejected the never-instantiated template with "no declared
# return type, and none could be inferred from its body".
def add_one(x):
    x + 1

def main() -> int32:
    println("{identity(5)}")
    println("{identity(true)}")
    println("{add_one(5)}")
    return 0
